        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ચેતવવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચેતવવું — cetavvũ — \"to warn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચોકીદારે મુસાફરોને ચેતવ્યા કે પુલ નબળો છે. cokīdāre musāphrone cetavyā ke pul nabḷo che. The watchman warned the passengers that the bridge was weak."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with તેણે (he or she …): તેણે બધાને ચેતવ્યા, teṇe badhāne cetavyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચેતવવું (cetavvũ) goes back to Sanskrit cētáyati, \"makes attentive, observes\" (CDIAL 4906): to make someone notice a danger. The person warned takes ને: મુસાફરોને ચેતવ્યા."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
